From 910db6982493339d2361e00e4dc20aad3321b139 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Refuse settled archive replay and prove terminal
 custody recovery fences

A retained containment marker routes archived tasks through the canonical archive service. Treat an authenticated archived local projection as a no-op before request metadata validation, preventing duplicate reason comments and changed-metadata errors. Preserve unknown-delivery request replay while the target remains triage.

Proof: duplicate archive regressions fail on 2f0d2bea8f with True/metadata refusal; four focused files pass 68 tests after the fix. Add independent reviewer custody, closure-payload, trigger-scope, reader and quarantine/rebuild/release regressions. Document permanently retained graph edges and the lack of dependent-owner notice.
